UI.CataTweaks.PactWarning_NAP=This action could break the mutual non-aggression pact with {0}.
UI.CataTweaks.PactWarning_Truce=This action could break the truce with {0}.
UI.CataTweaks.CouncilPoolYieldsToExpandedCouncil=Expanded Council is installed and manages the council, so this option is off and cannot be turned on while that mod is active.
UI.CataTweaks.StationShipyards={0} shipyards ({1} active)
UI.CataTweaks.StationSlots=Slots occupied: {0}/{1}
UI.CataTweaks.PooledConstructionSetting=One construction queue per station
UI.CataTweaks.PooledConstructionTooltip=All shipyards on a station share one ordered queue. Free compatible yards take the next ship at their own construction speed. Ships already building keep their progress.
UI.CataTweaks.StationBuildingYard={0}: {1} ({2} days)
UI.CataTweaks.StationYardState={0}: {1}
UI.CataTweaks.RallyNone=Rally: None
UI.CataTweaks.RallyFleet=Rally: {0}
UI.CataTweaks.RallyMissingFleet=Unavailable fleet
UI.CataTweaks.RallyHeadline=Ship rally
UI.CataTweaks.RallySummary={0} is rallying to {1}.
UI.CataTweaks.RallyDetail={0} ({1}), constructed at {2}, is rendezvousing with {3}, {4}.<br/>Departure: {5}<br/>Arrival: {6}<br/>Transfer delta-v: {7} km/s.<br/>The ship will merge with the fleet on arrival.
UI.CataTweaks.RallyJoined={0} joined {1}, {2}.
UI.CataTweaks.RallyNoDV=Automatic rally to {0} was not started: {1} has insufficient delta-v. The ship remains at {2}.
UI.CataTweaks.RallyUnavailable=Automatic rally to {0} could not be started. The ship remains at {1}.
UI.CataTweaks.RallyCommissioned={0} was built for a commission order of {1}. The automatic rally does not apply to it.
UI.CataTweaks.RallyReserveCleared={0} is mothballed in the reserve and cannot take new ships. Automatic rallies to this fleet are cleared.
TINotificationTemplate.displayName.CataTweaks_ShipRally=Ship rally
UI.CataTweaks.RallySetting=Automatic shipyard rally (experimental)
UI.CataTweaks.RallyTooltip=Requires One construction queue per station. Adds a fleet dropdown to station shipyard cards. Completed ships take the earliest affordable rendezvous and merge on arrival. Disabling this option stops new rallies; rallies already ordered finish normally.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.persistCampaignOptions.Label=Remember campaign options
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.persistCampaignOptions.Tooltip=Restores the last campaign's options and remembers custom faction names per faction.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.habTemplateNaming.Label=Hab template naming
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.habTemplateNaming.Tooltip=Applying a template adds its name and location to the hab name and copies its map icon. Saving recovers that template name and replaces the existing template.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.priorityPresetOverwrite.Label=Overwrite priority presets
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.priorityPresetOverwrite.Tooltip=Saving over a custom preset replaces it, updates control points using it, and preserves its default status.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.presetTrackingOnNationChanges.Label=Keep presets when priorities change
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.presetTrackingOnNationChanges.Tooltip=Reapplies the nation's preset when it gains or loses a priority.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.stationDividers.Label=Dividers between stations
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.stationDividers.Tooltip=Separates each station's shipyards with a line on the ship construction screen.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.fleetDetectionLocation.Label=Fleet detection location
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.fleetDetectionLocation.Tooltip=Fleet detection notices include the hab's orbit and body, or the body for landed fleets.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.nationCycleButtons.Label=Nation picker
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.nationCycleButtons.Tooltip=Adds an alphabetical nation dropdown and wraparound arrows for nations where you hold control points.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.unagedCouncilorPortraits.Label=Unchanging councilor portraits
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.unagedCouncilorPortraits.Tooltip=Councilors keep the same portrait, icon and video at every age.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.solarMirrorsBoostStations.Label=Solar mirrors boost stations
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.solarMirrorsBoostStations.Tooltip=Solar mirrors also power orbital stations inward of them. Surface bases and Lagrange point coverage are unchanged.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.solarMirrorOutputCap.Label=Solar mirror output cap
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.solarMirrorOutputCap.Tooltip=Maximum mirror-lit orbital solar output as a multiple of unlit output. Standard: 8. Surface bases are unaffected.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.expensiveFirstProjectReview.Label=Favor expensive missed projects
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.expensiveFirstProjectReview.Tooltip=Review Failed Projects weights availability chance by research cost, favoring expensive projects.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.betterLaunchSites.Label=Prefer better launch sites
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.betterLaunchSites.Tooltip=Boost can build in the eligible region nearest the equator. Occupied regions are excluded; the tooltip shows the eligible range.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.launchSiteFocus.Label=Launch site focus
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.launchSiteFocus.Tooltip=Share of Boost completions assigned to the best eligible region. 0% uses standard weighting; 100% always chooses the best site.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.factionDormancy.Label=Faction dormancy and return
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.factionDormancy.Tooltip=With Allow AI Factions To Be Disabled on, all human factions except yours can go dormant and return at two control points, without money, orgs or founding/event income.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.demandClaimDespiteOtherWars.Label=Demand Claim during other wars
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.demandClaimDespiteOtherWars.Tooltip=Only a war between the two nations blocks Demand Claim.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.inheritedCapitalClaims.Label=Borrow dormant nations' claims
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.inheritedCapitalClaims.Tooltip=Holding a dormant nation's original capital with a peaceful claim borrows its claims. Losing the capital or making its claim hostile removes them. Hostile borrowed claims can be legitimized at their source, one at a time. Projects that need the dormant nation can be offered. If several dormant nations share that capital, each of them lends its claims.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.dormantCapitalIdentity.Label=Restore dormant capital identity
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.dormantCapitalIdentity.Tooltip=After a war, a nation that lost its original capital to that enemy and now sits on a claimed dormant capital becomes that dormant nation. Regions, control points, priorities, stats, armies and resources transfer; diplomatic relations do not. Takes effect the next day at peace. A nation that joined it voluntarily is never the one it becomes.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.repeatableProjectScaling.Label=Repeatable project reward scaling
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.repeatableProjectScaling.Tooltip=Each prior completion adds this percentage of the base reward for repeatable capacity/resource projects. 0% restores flat rewards.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.tradeControlPoints.Label=Trade control points
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.tradeControlPoints.Tooltip=Adds control points by nation to diplomacy trades. The AI values them and can refuse a deal.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.controlPointTradeValue.Label=Control point trade value
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.controlPointTradeValue.Tooltip=Multiplies AI control point valuations. Higher values increase buying and selling prices. Abandoned nations' points have one tenth of the value.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.tradeSuppressedControlPoints.Label=Trade suppressed control points
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.tradeSuppressedControlPoints.Tooltip=Allows trading cracked-down and abandoned control points. The suppression and remaining duration transfer with them.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.friendlyPurge.Label=Purge friendly suppressed points
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.friendlyPurge.Tooltip=Purging a suppressed point of a faction with a pact or truce causes no anger and preserves the pact. Other purges still cause anger.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.warnOnPactBreak.Label=Warn before breaking a pact
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.warnOnPactBreak.Tooltip=Marks mission targets protected by a pact or truce and asks for confirmation before assignment.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.triggeredProjectsKeepAchievements.Label=Show Triggered Projects keeps achievements
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.triggeredProjectsKeepAchievements.Tooltip=This campaign option alone no longer counts as custom difficulty. Other options still affect victory achievements.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.spySlotsAsCouncilSlots.Label=New campaigns: shared councilor slots
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.spySlotsAsCouncilSlots.Tooltip=Sets the default for the campaign option that shares councilor and spy slots. Existing campaigns are unaffected.
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.restoredEmpires.Label=New campaigns: Restored Empires
UI.CataTweaks.Setting.restoredEmpires.Tooltip=Sets the default for Restored Empires Claims. Existing campaigns are unaffected.
UI.CataTweaks.SectionUI=Quality of Life and UI
UI.CataTweaks.RenameTo=Rename to {0}
UI.CataTweaks.RepeatingScaled=This is a repeatable project. Each repeat adds {0}{1} to its research cost and {2} of its base reward to its reward. Our next attempt will cost {3}{1} and grant {4}.
UI.CataTweaks.LegitimizeBorrowedClaims=Sufficient investment in the Government and Unity priorities will make the borrowed claim on {0} peaceful for its source nation. It remains borrowed and is lost if we lose the lending capital. Current progress: {1}/{2} <color=#FFFFFFFF><sprite name="investments"></color>.
UI.CataTweaks.Campaign.councilPool.Label=Spy Slots Become Councilor Slots
UI.CataTweaks.Campaign.councilPool.Tooltip=Councilors and turned councilors share a pool of eight slots: no spies allows eight councilors, two spies allows six. The seventh and eighth slots require {0} and {1}, after {2}. When disabled, both projects are hidden.
UI.CataTweaks.Campaign.restoredEmpires.Label=Restored Empires Claims
UI.CataTweaks.Campaign.restoredEmpires.Tooltip=Adds British and Liberian restoration claims in every scenario. In Broken Earth Scenario, Rome gains six independent regional conquest projects: continental Europe, Africa, India, North America, South America and Asia. Each requires Great Nations, costs 35,000 research points and grants +10 Control Point Capacity (210,000 research points and +60 capacity in total). Foreign Roman claims are hostile; the Italian core is peaceful. When disabled, these projects are hidden and the mod’s claims are inactive.
